@startuml
title AsyncTask — cooperative cancellation
<style>
document {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BoxPadding 10
  ParticipantPadding 10
}
title {
  FontSize 16
  FontColor #111111
}
</style>

actor "Owner" as Owner
participant "AsyncTask<T>" as Task
participant "Task promise" as Promise
participant "Running coroutine" as Coroutine
participant "CancellationToken<T>" as Token
participant "Awaiting consumer" as Consumer

Owner -> Task : cancel() or release owning task
Task -> Promise : set atomic cancellation flag
note over Promise,Coroutine
  Cancellation is a request, not forced interruption.
  It does not destroy or forcibly resume the coroutine frame.
end note

alt Coroutine reaches a cancellationPoint
  Coroutine -> Promise : inspect cancellation flag
  Promise --> Coroutine : cancellation observed
  Coroutine -> Coroutine : follow cancellation-aware path
else Coroutine does not check cancellation
  Coroutine -> Coroutine : continues executing normally
end

opt Consumer awaits via CancellationToken
  Token -> Task : await task completion
  Task -> Consumer : AsyncResult<T> includes cancellation status
  Token -> Consumer : mark returned result as canceled
end

note over Owner,Consumer
  Cancellation signaling is cooperative. Code must observe the token /
  cancellation result and decide how to stop or clean up.
end note
@enduml
